arguments.prompt:
You are implementing a Blazor Web App for a logistics company that tracks shipments. The project has already been scaffolded at `/tmp/sv-1636b31c210043f9b676e49aebc06fcb/ShipmentTracker/` with `dotnet new blazor -int Auto -ai -au Individual`.

The project structure:
- `ShipmentTracker/` - server project
- `ShipmentTracker.Client/` - WebAssembly client project

Server Program.cs already has Identity, EF Core (SQLite), and Auto render mode configured.
Client Program.cs has auth state deserialization.

## Requirements
1. Dispatchers view a list of shipments with status and destination
2. Customers check their shipment status and estimated delivery
3. Interactive Auto global mode (already configured)
4. Individual accounts auth (already configured)

## What to implement

### Step 1: Remove default template pages
Delete these files from `ShipmentTracker.Client/Pages/`:
- Counter.razor
- Weather.razor

Keep Home.razor but replace its content with a welcome/landing page for the shipment tracker.
Keep Auth.razor and NotFound.razor as-is.

### Step 2: Create shared models in `ShipmentTracker.Client/Models/Shipment.cs`
Create a `ShipmentTracker.Client/Models/` directory with a `Shipment.cs` file:

```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public class Shipment
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string TrackingNumber { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Origin { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Destination { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public ShipmentStatus Status { get; set; }
    public DateTime ShippedDate { get; set; }
    public DateTime EstimatedDelivery { get; set; }
    public string CustomerEmail { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Description { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}

public enum ShipmentStatus
{
    Pending,
    PickedUp,
    InTransit,
    OutForDelivery,
    Delivered,
    Delayed
}
```

### Step 3: Create service interface in `ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/IShipmentService.cs`

```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public interface IShipmentService
{
    Task<List<Shipment>> GetAllShipmentsAsync();
    Task<Shipment?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber);
    Task<List<Shipment>> GetShipmentsByCustomerAsync(string customerEmail);
    Task<Shipment> UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus status);
    Task<Shipment> CreateShipmentAsync(Shipment shipment);
}
```

### Step 4: Create client-side HTTP implementation in `ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/ShipmentHttpService.cs`

```csharp
using System.Net.Http.Json;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

public class ShipmentHttpService : IShipmentService
{
    private readonly HttpClient _http;

    public ShipmentHttpService(HttpClient http)
    {
        _http = http;
    }

    public async Task<List<Shipment>> GetAllShipmentsAsync()
    {
        return await _http.GetFromJsonAsync<List<Shipment>>("api/shipments") ?? [];
    }

    public async Task<Shipment?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber)
    {
        return await _http.GetFromJsonAsync<Shipment?>($"api/shipments/track/{trackingNumber}");
    }

    public async Task<List<Shipment>> GetShipmentsByCustomerAsync(string customerEmail)
    {
        return await _http.GetFromJsonAsync<List<Shipment>>($"api/shipments/customer/{Uri.EscapeDataString(customerEmail)}") ?? [];
    }

    public async Task<Shipment> UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus status)
    {
        var response = await _http.PutAsJsonAsync($"api/shipments/{id}/status", status);
        response.EnsureSuccessStatusCode();
        return await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<Shipment>() ?? throw new Exception("Failed to update shipment");
    }

    public async Task<Shipment> CreateShipmentAsync(Shipment shipment)
    {
        var response = await _http.PostAsJsonAsync("api/shipments", shipment);
        response.EnsureSuccessStatusCode();
        return await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<Shipment>() ?? throw new Exception("Failed to create shipment");
    }
}
```

### Step 5: Register HttpClient and service in Client Program.cs

Update `ShipmentTracker.Client/Program.cs` to:

```csharp
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.WebAssembly.Hosting;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

var builder = WebAssemblyHostBuilder.CreateDefault(args);

builder.Services.AddAuthorizationCore();
builder.Services.AddCascadingAuthenticationState();
builder.Services.AddAuthenticationStateDeserialization();

builder.Services.AddHttpClient("ShipmentTracker.ServerAPI", client =>
    client.BaseAddress = new Uri(builder.HostEnvironment.BaseAddress));
builder.Services.AddScoped(sp => sp.GetRequiredService<IHttpClientFactory>().CreateClient("ShipmentTracker.ServerAPI"));
builder.Services.AddScoped<IShipmentService, ShipmentHttpService>();

await builder.Build().RunAsync();
```

### Step 6: Create server-side service implementation

Create `ShipmentTracker/Services/ShipmentServerService.cs`:

```csharp
using Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;
using ShipmentTracker.Data;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Services;

public class ShipmentServerService : IShipmentService
{
    private readonly ApplicationDbContext _db;

    public ShipmentServerService(ApplicationDbContext db)
    {
        _db = db;
    }

    public async Task<List<Shipment>> GetAllShipmentsAsync()
    {
        return await _db.Shipments.OrderByDescending(s => s.ShippedDate).ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task<Shipment?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber)
    {
        return await _db.Shipments.FirstOrDefaultAsync(s => s.TrackingNumber == trackingNumber);
    }

    public async Task<List<Shipment>> GetShipmentsByCustomerAsync(string customerEmail)
    {
        return await _db.Shipments
            .Where(s => s.CustomerEmail == customerEmail)
            .OrderByDescending(s => s.ShippedDate)
            .ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task<Shipment> UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus status)
    {
        var shipment = await _db.Shipments.FindAsync(id)
            ?? throw new KeyNotFoundException($"Shipment {id} not found");
        shipment.Status = status;
        await _db.SaveChangesAsync();
        return shipment;
    }

    public async Task<Shipment> CreateShipmentAsync(Shipment shipment)
    {
        _db.Shipments.Add(shipment);
        await _db.SaveChangesAsync();
        return shipment;
    }
}
```

### Step 7: Add Shipment DbSet to ApplicationDbContext

The file is at `ShipmentTracker/Data/ApplicationDbContext.cs`. Add:
```csharp
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;
```
And add the property:
```csharp
public DbSet<Shipment> Shipments => Set<Shipment>();
```

### Step 8: Create API endpoints

Create `ShipmentTracker/Endpoints/ShipmentEndpoints.cs`:

```csharp
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Endpoints;

public static class ShipmentEndpoints
{
    public static void MapShipmentEndpoints(this WebApplication app)
    {
        var group = app.MapGroup("api/shipments").RequireAuthorization();

        group.MapGet("", async (IShipmentService service) =>
            Results.Ok(await service.GetAllShipmentsAsync()));

        group.MapGet("track/{trackingNumber}", async (string trackingNumber, IShipmentService service) =>
        {
            var shipment = await service.GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(trackingNumber);
            return shipment is null ? Results.NotFound() : Results.Ok(shipment);
        });

        group.MapGet("customer/{email}", async (string email, IShipmentService service) =>
            Results.Ok(await service.GetShipmentsByCustomerAsync(Uri.UnescapeDataString(email))));

        group.MapPost("", async (Shipment shipment, IShipmentService service) =>
            Results.Ok(await service.CreateShipmentAsync(shipment)));

        group.MapPut("{id}/status", async (int id, [FromBody] ShipmentStatus status, IShipmentService service) =>
            Results.Ok(await service.UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(id, status)));
    }
}
```

### Step 9: Register server service and map endpoints in server Program.cs

In `ShipmentTracker/Program.cs`, add after the existing service registrations (after `AddSingleton<IEmailSender...>`):
```csharp
builder.Services.AddScoped<IShipmentService, ShipmentServerService>();
```

And before `app.Run();`, add:
```csharp
app.MapShipmentEndpoints();
```

You'll also need these usings at the top:
```csharp
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;
using ShipmentTracker.Services;
using ShipmentTracker.Endpoints;
```

### Step 10: Create pages in the Client project

**Replace `ShipmentTracker.Client/Pages/Home.razor`:**
```razor
@page "/"

<PageTitle>ShipmentTracker - Home</PageTitle>

<h1>Shipment Tracker</h1>
<p>Welcome to the logistics shipment tracking system.</p>

<AuthorizeView>
    <Authorized>
        <p>You are signed in as <strong>@context.User.Identity?.Name</strong>.</p>
        <div class="d-flex gap-3 mt-3">
            <a href="shipments" class="btn btn-primary">View All Shipments</a>
            <a href="my-shipments" class="btn btn-outline-primary">My Shipments</a>
            <a href="track" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">Track a Shipment</a>
        </div>
    </Authorized>
    <NotAuthorized>
        <p>Please <a href="Account/Login">sign in</a> to track your shipments.</p>
    </NotAuthorized>
</AuthorizeView>
```

**Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Pages/Shipments.razor`** (Dispatcher view):
```razor
@page "/shipments"
@using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models
@using ShipmentTracker.Client.Services
@inject IShipmentService ShipmentService
@attribute [Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization.Authorize]

<PageTitle>All Shipments</PageTitle>

<h1>Shipments</h1>

<div class="mb-3 d-flex gap-2 align-items-end">
    <div>
        <label class="form-label">Filter by Status</label>
        <select class="form-select" @bind="statusFilter">
