2. Customers check their shipment status and estimated delivery
3. Interactive Auto global mode (already configured)
4. Individual accounts auth (already configured)

## What to implement

### Step 1: Remove default template pages
Delete these files from `ShipmentTracker.Client/Pages/`:
- Counter.razor
- Weather.razor

Keep Home.razor but replace its content with a welcome/landing page for the shipment tracker.
Keep Auth.razor and NotFound.razor as-is.

### Step 2: Create shared models in `ShipmentTracker.Client/Models/Shipment.cs`
Create a `ShipmentTracker.Client/Models/` directory with a `Shipment.cs` file:

```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public class Shipment
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string TrackingNumber { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Origin { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Destination { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public ShipmentStatus Status { get; set; }
    public DateTime ShippedDate { get; set; }
    public DateTime EstimatedDelivery { get; set; }
    public string CustomerEmail { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Description { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}

public enum ShipmentStatus
{
    Pending,
    PickedUp,
    InTransit,
    OutForDelivery,
    Delivered,
    Delayed
}
```

